Tool.
  tool """" KeYmaera X """"
  model """" ArchiveEntry "3-Machine pH D2<0: box descent V-dot<=0 on c1,c2 in [4/5,1], PARAMETRIC in d"

/*
 * KeYmaera X STATUS: PROVED (qed=1, ~0.34s). V' <= 0 on the large-signal box
 * c1,c2 in [4/5,1] for ALL d in (0,3/20] -- the multilinear step that
 * theorem_3machine_descent_parametric formerly left as prose.
 *
 * PROOF (abstract sign-assembly, sidestepping the box QE that times out):
 * sympy shows V' is SEPARABLE-AFFINE in (c1,c2): coeff(c1*c2)=0, so
 *   V' = c1*P(rest) + c2*Q(rest) + R(rest),
 * and on the box it is the exact convex combination of the 4 corner values
 *   V' = wAA*V'(4/5,4/5) + wAB*V'(4/5,1) + wBA*V'(1,4/5) + wBB*V'(1,1),
 * with barycentric weights wAA=(5-5c1)(5-5c2), wAB=(5-5c1)(5c2-4),
 * wBA=(5c1-4)(5-5c2), wBB=(5c1-4)(5c2-4), each >=0 on the box and summing to 1
 * (sympy: identity residual = 0; weight sum = 1, both machine-checked).
 * The 4 corner forms are NSD for d in (0,3/20] (theorem_3machine_descent_parametric,
 * PROVED). We cut the abstract lemma
 *   forall w.. n.. VV ((all w>=0 & all n<=0 & VV=sum w*n) -> VV<=0)
 * (lemma_sign_assembly), instantiate it (allL) with the explicit weights, the
 * explicit corner polynomials, and V' itself, then discharge the 9-conjunct
 * premise by per-conjunct QE: 4 weight signs (linear), 4 corner NSDs (the proven
 * QEs), and the interpolation identity (proved standalone in 120ms). Z3 never has
 * to do the monolithic box QE (which OOM-kills even WITH the corners as
 * hypotheses -- confirmed): each leaf is small. This is the decomposition the
 * old header described as "NOT machine-closed"; the missing piece was that the
 * IDENTITY had to be supplied as the lemma's VV-binding (so Z3 checks it as one
 * cheap equality) rather than re-derived inside the product expansion.
 *
 * Negative control: widening the band to d<=1 (corner (1,1) ceases to be NSD)
 * makes the corner-conjunct QE FAIL -> whole proof fails, confirming non-vacuity.
 */

ProgramVariables
  Real w1; Real w2; Real w3; Real s1; Real s2; Real c1; Real c2; Real d;
End.

Problem
  \forall d \forall w1 \forall w2 \forall w3 \forall s1 \forall s2 \forall c1 \forall c2 (
    ( 0 < d & d <= 3/20 & 4/5 <= c1 & c1 <= 1 & 4/5 <= c2 & c2 <= 1 )
    -> (c1*d*w1^2 - c1*d*w1*w2/4 - 3*c1*d*w2^2/4 + 2*c1*s1*w1/5 - 2*c1*s1*w2/5 + c1*w1^2 - 3*c1*w1*w2/4 - c1*w2^2/4 - 3*c2*d*w2^2/4 - c2*d*w2*w3/4 + c2*d*w3^2 + 2*c2*s2*w2/5 - 2*c2*s2*w3/5 - c2*w2^2/4 - 3*c2*w2*w3/4 + c2*w3^2 + 3*d^2*s1*w2/4 - 3*d^2*s2*w2/4 - d*s1^2/4 - 3*d*s1*s2/2 - d*s1*w1 + d*s1*w2/4 - d*s2^2/4 - d*s2*w2/4 + d*s2*w3 + 2*d*w2^2 - 3*s1^2/4 - s1*s2/2 - s1*w1 - 3*s2^2/4 + s2*w3 - 2*w1^2 - 2*w3^2) <= 0 )
End.

